{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,4]],"date-time":"2025-11-04T10:52:46Z","timestamp":1762253566058,"version":"3.37.3"},"reference-count":49,"publisher":"The Royal Society","issue":"10","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,10,1]],"date-time":"2020-10-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1601510400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,10,1]],"date-time":"2020-10-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1601510400000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000616","name":"Fisheries Society of the British Isles","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["Small research grant"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["Small research grant"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000616","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000268","name":"Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["BB\/M011151\/1"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["BB\/M011151\/1"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000268","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]},{"name":"Genetics Society","award":["Heredity fieldwork grant"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["Heredity fieldwork grant"]}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["royalsocietypublishing.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["R. Soc. open sci."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Tetrapods and fish have adapted distinct carbamoyl-phosphate synthase (CPS) enzymes to initiate the ornithine urea cycle during the detoxification of nitrogenous wastes. We report evidence that in the ureotelic subgenus of extremophile fish<jats:italic>Oreochromis Alcolapia<\/jats:italic>, CPS III has undergone convergent evolution and adapted its substrate affinity to ammonia, which is typical of terrestrial vertebrate CPS I. Unusually, unlike in other vertebrates, the expression of CPS III in<jats:italic>Alcolapia<\/jats:italic>is localized to the skeletal muscle and is activated in the myogenic lineage during early embryonic development with expression remaining in mature fish. We propose that adaptation in<jats:italic>Alcolapia<\/jats:italic>included both convergent evolution of CPS function to that of terrestrial vertebrates, as well as changes in development mechanisms redirecting<jats:italic>CPS III<\/jats:italic>gene expression to the skeletal muscle.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1098\/rsos.201200","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,10,14]],"date-time":"2020-10-14T07:05:59Z","timestamp":1602659159000},"page":"201200","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1098\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":7,"title":["Adaptation of the carbamoyl-phosphate synthetase enzyme in an extremophile fish"],"prefix":"10.1098","volume":"7","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8764-2051","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Lewis J.","family":"White","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Biology Department, University of York, York YO10 5DD, UK"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0459-0912","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Gemma","family":"Sutton","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Biology Department, University of York, York YO10 5DD, UK"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Asilatu","family":"Shechonge","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tanzania Fisheries Research Institute, PO BOX 98, Kyela, Mbeya, Tanzania"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Julia J.","family":"Day","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Genetics, Evolution and Environment, University College London, Darwin Building, Gower Street, London WC1E 6BT, UK"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Kanchon K.","family":"Dasmahapatra","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Biology Department, University of York, York YO10 5DD, UK"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mary E.","family":"Pownall","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Biology Department, University of York, York YO10 5DD, UK"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"175","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,10,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_3_7_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"273","DOI":"10.1242\/jeb.198.2.273","article-title":"Nitrogen excretion: three end products, many physiological roles","volume":"198","author":"Wright PA","year":"1995","journal-title":"J. Exp. Biol."},{"key":"e_1_3_7_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1242\/jeb.140210"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1242\/jeb.00956"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2155","DOI":"10.1242\/jeb.204.12.2155","article-title":"Pathways for urea production during early life of an air-breathing teleost, the African catfish Clarias gariepinus Burchell","volume":"204","author":"Terjesen BF","year":"2001","journal-title":"J. Exp. Biol."},{"key":"e_1_3_7_6_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF00043929"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_7_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"329","DOI":"10.1242\/jeb.114.1.329","article-title":"An analysis of branchial ammonia excretion in the freshwater rainbow trout: effects of environmental pH change and sodium uptake blockade","volume":"114","author":"Wright PA","year":"1985","journal-title":"J. Exp. Biol."},{"key":"e_1_3_7_8_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.ympev.2019.04.008"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_9_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/337165a0"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_10_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1086\/422054"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_11_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/366146a0"},{"key":"e_1_3_7_12_2